## Pipeline (as of 2026-09-02)

- Pruned to `00`–`10`. Deleted: the SWIM `06.x` series with `roles/swim` + `roles/http_image_server` + `image_servers` inventory; `deploy_yangsuite.yml` with `roles/yangsuite_docker` + `yangsuite_servers`; the config backup stage with `roles/backup_configs`, `config-backups/`, `group_vars/iosxe|nxos`, `inventory/cml.yml` and `platform_groups.yml`; and the verify preflight play. Survivors were renumbered to close the gaps. Stage numbers below use the new scheme.
- Inventory is now `static_inventory.yml` only — two groups, `catalyst_center` (localhost → CatC API, stages `01`–`09`) and `campus_evpn` (three switches over SSH, stage `10`). No CML, no `.env`. `cisco.cml`/`cisco.nxos`/`virl2_client` dropped from the evpn requirements files.
- Ran on Kali: `01`–`05`, `06`–`09`, and the verify play. Do not re-run `08`/`09` against the live lab until asked.
- `01`: skip building/floor UPDATE (`site_hierarchy_update_existing: false`). `cisco.catalystcenter.buildings` PUT raises `UnboundLocalError: local variable 'func'`. Re-enable with `-e site_hierarchy_update_existing=true`.
- `03`: bind live Design names, do not CREATE duplicates. Live: CLI `CLI Admin`, SNMP `SNMPv2c Read`/`SNMPv2c Write`, NETCONF `defaultNetConfPort` (830), HTTP `HTTPS Read`/`HTTPS Write`. Each project row `assign_credentials.site_name` = that site’s MAIN path.
- `08`: three passes. `POST /dna/intent/api/v1/sda/provisionDevices` cannot set wireless DeviceInfo (`NCWL10092`). `roles/provision_devices/tasks/provision_site.yml` defers `family` containing `Wireless` to `provision_wireless.yml`, which provisions the WLC and sets its managed AP locations. `provision_accesspoints.yml` then names and site-assigns APs. Site-105 9300s provisioned 3/3. The WLC pass forces by default: `force_provisioning` comes from `force_wireless_provisioning` (role `defaults/main.yml`, default **true**), deliberately separate from the wired `force_reprovision` so forcing the controller does not also PUT-re-push the fabric switches. Forcing is the default because the module short-circuits on "already provisioned" without diffing intent, so a changed `managed_ap_locations` would otherwise never land. Disable with `-e force_wireless_provisioning=false`. Gates: `wireless_provision_enabled`, `ap_provision_enabled`.
- Every WLC provisioning write goes through `provision_workflow_manager` (`provision_wireless.yml`, and the AP-takeover re-provision in `provision_accesspoints.yml`). The only direct provisioning REST calls are the wired `POST`/`PUT /sda/provisionDevices` in `provision_site.yml`, and both payloads share one classification, `_wireless_ips`, so `-e force_reprovision=true` cannot route a controller at the SDA API. Remaining `uri` calls in the wireless paths are read-only GETs (family lookup, `family=Unified AP` listing, site membership). Deferral matches `wireless_family_markers` (role `defaults/main.yml`) as substrings — `Unified AP` needs its own marker because an AP's family contains no "Wireless".
- **AP provisioning is a real, separate CatC action, and stage 08 now does it (Step G of `provision_accesspoints.yml`, verified live 2026-09-03).** Provisioning the WLC creates the WLAN and policy profiles; the tags that bind an AP to those profiles are created only when the AP itself is provisioned. That is Step 34 "Provision the AP" of "Provision a Cisco Catalyst 9800 Series Wireless Controller", which points at "Provision Cisco APs on day 1" (Inventory → select APs → Actions → Provision → Provision Device → Assign Site to a **floor** → Configuration for AP zone / RF profile → Deploy). Guide: `m_provision-wireless-devices.html#id_91719`.
- That wizard's Assign Site step notes CatC does **not** set that site as the AP *location* during provisioning (separate Configure APs workflow) — which is why an AP's `network-device` record keeps `siteHierarchy: null` even after everything succeeds.
- Naming the AP, `assign_device_to_site` and a forced WLC re-provision are inventory membership plus a controller re-push. They are **not** the AP provision action and do not create the AP's policy/site tag — that was the gap. The earlier note claiming CatC cannot provision an AP was wrong.
- `rfProfileName` is **required** on the provision call. Without it CatC returns `NCWS14003` "RF Profile is required for default/empty AP Zone". This CatC ships LOW/TYPICAL/HIGH with **none** flagged `defaultRfProfile`, so there is nothing to inherit; the role resolves `access_points[].rf_profile` → the profile flagged default → `ap_default_rf_profile` (defaults `TYPICAL`).
- Idempotency comes from `GET /dna/intent/api/v1/wireless/accesspoint-configuration/summary?key=<Ethernet MAC>` and its `provisioningStatus` boolean. Provision only when false, or when `-e force_reprovision=true`. Re-running otherwise would bounce the AP.
- Verified end to end on 2026-09-03: `provisioningStatus` false → true, AP mode flipped to `FlexConnect`, and on the WLC `SITE-105-AP-1` moved off the three default tags onto `ST_Durha_Site-105_d97a1_0` / `PT_Durha_Site-_MAIN_70ab7` / `TYPICAL` (source Static), with that policy tag mapping `PSEUDOCO-FLEX-Profile` — the WLAN carrying `PSEUDOCO-POD12`. A second run reported "already provisioned" and changed nothing.
- `provision_workflow_manager` genuinely cannot do it: it types by family and maps only `Wireless Controller` and `Switches and Hubs`/`Routers`, so `Unified AP` falls through. `accesspoint_workflow_manager` *can* (`wireless.ap_provision`), but when `site` is set it first calls `verify_wlc_provision` → `sda.get_device_info`, and on the exception a non-fabric WLC raises it calls `check_return_status()` and aborts the whole module. That module bug is why `site` was stripped and AP provisioning was lost entirely.
- **The module to use is `cisco.catalystcenter.wireless_access_points_provision`, but only from collection `2.11.0` or newer.** It takes `siteId` + `networkDevices` (`deviceId`, optional `meshRole`/`beamState`) plus optional `rfProfileName`/`apZoneName`, and has no SDA gate. Requires bumping the `cisco.catalystcenter` pin from 2.10.2.
- The pin matters because the collection/SDK pairing is version-sensitive. In `catalystcentersdk` 3.1.3.0.1 (all three profiles), `ap_provision` → `POST /dna/intent/api/v1/wirelessAccessPoints/provision` (kwargs `siteId`/`networkDevices`), while `ap_provision_connectivity` → `POST /dna/intent/api/v1/wireless/ap-provision`, whose validator schema is an **array** of `{deviceName, rfProfile, siteNameHierarchy, type}` and whose signature is `(headers, payload, ...)`. Collections call `func(**params)` with no reshaping, so a module wired to the wrong one sends the options as query params against an empty `[]` body.
- `cisco.catalystcenter` 2.10.2 and `cisco.dnac` at both 6.46.0 and 6.51.0 wire `wireless_access_points_provision` to `ap_provision_connectivity` — broken. Only `cisco.catalystcenter` 2.11.0 wires it to `ap_provision`. Do not reach for the `cisco.dnac` copy of this module.
- `wireless_provision_access_point` is the old API and cannot substitute: its argspec declares `payload` as a list, but the `ap_provision` it calls runs `check_type(payload, dict)`.
- `accesspoint_workflow_manager` cannot do the site assignment here: given a `site` key it calls `verify_wlc_provision` → `sda/get_device_info`, and the non-fabric WLC has no fabric role, so it 400s and aborts the stage. Use it for name/location/mode only, and `assign_device_to_site` (as stage 05 does) for the assignment. `provision_workflow_manager` is not an option for an AP either — it types by family and maps only `Wireless Controller`/`Switches and Hubs`/`Routers`, so `Unified AP` falls through. `accesspoint_location_workflow_manager` is floor-map X/Y/Z only.
- An AP's `network-device` record keeps `siteHierarchy: null` even once assigned. Read membership from the site side: `GET /dna/intent/api/v1/site-member/{siteId}/member?memberType=networkdevice`.
- AP MAC gotcha: CatC indexes an AP by **radio** MAC (`macAddress`), not Ethernet (`apEthernetMacAddress`). `?macAddress=<eth>` returns 0 devices and the module resolves APs through that same query. `lab_ap_macs` holds the Ethernet MAC (what the student can read); `provision_accesspoints.yml` lists `family=Unified AP` and translates. Site-105-AP-1: eth `04:5f:b9:ca:03:58` → radio `68:7d:b4:90:95:00`.
- Live WLC `198.18.5.103` as of 2026-09-03 (note: `lab_access['C9800-WLC']` says `.102`, which is wrong — `.102` is DNS/AD): WLAN 1 `DCLOUD-XAR-FLEX-Profile` SSID `PSEUDOCO-POD#` (dCloud pre-built, never renamed) and WLAN 17 `PSEUDOCO-FLEX-Profile` SSID `PSEUDOCO-POD12` (pushed by our stage 07). Pre-built tags `DCLOUD-XAR-FLEX-PT`/`FLEX-SITE` exist but CatC created none of its own. AP `SITE-105-AP-1` was Registered, already named, `siteHierarchy: None`, on all three default tags. Going CatC-native puts the AP on CatC-generated tags serving `PSEUDOCO-POD12` and leaves the dCloud WLAN and tags dormant — which is what happened once Step G landed. Note the AP's `location` reads `default location` on both CatC and the WLC even though stage 08 passes `Leaf1`; per the guide, AP location is the separate Configure APs workflow and is not set by provisioning.
- `09` queues only `DayNTemplateNames` with `DeployTemplate: true`. Site-105 was flipped to `true` so the play would not assert-empty. CatC reported SUCCESS (`5d38a5da-561e-40fa-b00b-563ef5ab4eab`) for `172.30.255.1–3`.
- Overlay **is** live as of 2026-09-03. Leaf1 `198.18.128.22`: VRFs Main/PROD/IOT with RDs `172.30.255.1:10|101|102` and Vlan10/101/102 + Vlan1010/1101/1102; NVE peers UP to `.2` and `.3` (L3CP for all three L3VNIs, L2CP 100010 to `.2`); EVPN BGP to RR `172.30.255.3` Established, 31 prefixes, 38 network entries. Came up Sep 2 14:36, so an earlier push landed it — the previous note that CatC reported SUCCESS while the CLI was absent (`% BGP not active`) was true at that time but is now stale. Still verify on the box; SUCCESS alone proves nothing.
- `maximum-paths ibgp 1` never appears in running-config (it is the IOS default), so the `{% if DEFN_NODE_ROLES[...] | length > 1 %}` guards in `FABRIC-EVPN.j2`/`FABRIC-OVERLAY.j2` only suppress a no-op line. `ip ssh version 2` was dropped from `FABRIC-NAC.j2` and is likewise absent from the box.

## CatC Jinja UDV scanner

- Static scan ignores `{% set %}` inside `{% for %}`. Dummy-declare loop vars at template scope (already done for `vrf`).
- `default((L3VNIOFFSET|string) + vrf.id)` does not parse as a declaration. Bare `{{ l3_vni }}` becomes a required Template Hub input (“Value should not be empty”).
- Site-105 `DEFN-VRF.j2` already has explicit `l3_vlan` / `l3_vni`. Prefer `{{ vrf['l3_vni'] }}` over a local `l3_vni`. `FABRIC-NVE.j2` was fixed locally; **not yet re-synced with `06`**.
